    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25998" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διασχημᾰτ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shape, form variously,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.1.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.4993
			</span></i>:— 
				Med.
			, of God, <i>mould as Creator,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				53b
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				50c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> simply,
				<i>shape, model,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Icar.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Prom.</u>
				11
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>shape oneself, prepare,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>Hist.</u>
					p.269D.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
